Add a real per-language byte breakdown to the Ship tab (GitHub Languages-bar equivalent)

Walks the active project's real files on disk and sums actual byte
sizes per language via a new languageBreakdown.js module - never
estimates from file/line counts. Excludes dependency/build dirs and
machine-generated files (lockfiles, .min.js, source maps, .d.ts,
*.generated.*), same as GitHub's own Linguist. Minor languages (<1%)
fold into a real 'Other' bucket, same as GitHub's display. Renders as
a colored segmented bar + legend using GitHub's actual Linguist colors,
auto-refreshing when the Ship tab opens. Verified with real smoke tests
(this repo, an empty dir, a dir with only excluded files, a missing
path) plus the full 60-test suite.
